{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "page": 1,
      "type": "title",
      "text": "Drug A Versus Placebo in Hypertension: a Randomized Controlled Trial",
      "section": null
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Methods",
      "section": "Methods"
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This was a multicentre, double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled trial. Adults aged 18 years or older with hypertension were eligible. Exclusion criteria included pregnancy and severe renal disease. A total of 238 patients were randomly assigned in a 1:1 ratio to receive Drug A 10 mg once daily (n = 120) or placebo (n = 118). Patients were followed for 12 months. The primary outcome was major cardiovascular events at 12 months. Secondary outcomes included all-cause death and change in systolic blood pressure. Analyses followed the intention-to-treat principle.",
      "section": "Methods"
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Results",
      "section": "Results"
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Of the 238 randomized patients, 230 were included in the analysis. The primary outcome occurred in 24 of 120 patients (20.0%) in the Drug A group and 36 of 118 patients (30.5%) in the placebo group (hazard ratio 0.62, 95% CI 0.41 to 0.94; P = 0.02). In the per-protocol population, the adjusted hazard ratio was 0.60 (95% CI 0.39 to 0.93). Systolic blood pressure decreased by 8.1 ± 13.2 mm Hg with Drug A.",
      "section": "Results"
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Table 1. Baseline characteristics of the participants",
      "section": "Results"
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Table 2. Outcomes at 12 months (intention-to-treat population)",
      "section": "Results"
    }
